# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These hold team names AND their six-digit secret codes in plaintext. The code
# is the ONLY thing protecting a team's encrypted work (19.9 bits — see the
# entropy note in teacher.html), and this repository is public. Committing them
# would let anyone overwrite those teams.
#
# The audit teams are throwaway and hold no student work, so this is hygiene
# rather than an incident — but the same files exist for real classes, and a
# rule that only sometimes applies is not a rule.
teams.json
audit-*/

# ── Run outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The PILOT's images are committed on purpose: they are the evidence for the
# findings, and a reviewer cannot check the calibration argument without seeing
# them. 18 images is ~46 MB.
#
# A FULL run is 3,060 images ≈ 7.9 GB and must never enter git history. Point
# `--images-dir` outside the repo for real runs, or use external storage. If
# that ever lands here by accident it is not removable by a later commit.
out/*/images/
*.large/
